  "knowledge_base": [
    {"id": "KB-01", "topic": "Charging", "question": "How should I charge my car day to day?", "answer": "For daily driving keep the battery between 20% and 80% and use AC charging at home or work. Charge to 100% before long trips. DC fast charging is safe to use whenever you need it; the car manages battery temperature automatically. Set a charge limit in the ZEEKR app under Energy > Charging."},
    {"id": "KB-02", "topic": "Charging", "question": "How do I precondition the battery for fast charging?", "answer": "Set a DC fast charger as your navigation destination and the car warms or cools the battery automatically on the way. You can also start preconditioning manually under Energy > Battery Preconditioning. Preconditioning can noticeably cut charging time in cold weather."},
    {"id": "KB-03", "topic": "Range", "question": "Why is my range lower in winter?", "answer": "Cold temperatures reduce battery efficiency and cabin heating uses energy. Precondition the cabin while plugged in, use seat and steering-wheel heating, and keep tyres at the recommended pressure. A 15-30% drop in winter range is normal."},
    {"id": "KB-04", "topic": "Software", "question": "How do over-the-air (OTA) updates work?", "answer": "When an update is available you get a notification in the car and the ZEEKR app. Install it while parked with at least 30% charge; the car can't be driven during installation (about 30-40 minutes). You can schedule it overnight from the centre display under Settings > Software."},
    {"id": "KB-05", "topic": "Warranty", "question": "What does the warranty cover?", "answer": "The vehicle warranty covers manufacturing defects in materials and workmanship. The high-voltage battery warranty covers defects and capacity loss below the stated minimum health threshold. Wear items (tyres, wiper blades, brake pads), accident damage and misuse aren't covered. Exact terms vary by market."},
    {"id": "KB-06", "topic": "Roadside", "question": "What does roadside assistance include?", "answer": "24/7 help for breakdowns, flat tyres, flat batteries, lockouts and running out of charge, including towing to the nearest ZEEKR service centre or charger when needed. It is included for the roadside assistance period of your warranty."},
    {"id": "KB-07", "topic": "Tyres", "question": "What tyre pressure should I use?", "answer": "The recommended cold tyre pressures are on the label in the driver's door frame and on the centre display under Vehicle > Tyres. For most ZEEKR models this is 2.7-3.0 bar. Check pressures monthly and before long trips."},
    {"id": "KB-08", "topic": "Digital key", "question": "How do I share my digital key?", "answer": "Open the ZEEKR app, go to Vehicle > Digital Key > Share, and choose the person, access level and time period. They'll need the ZEEKR app and an account. You can revoke access at any time."},
    {"id": "KB-09", "topic": "Maintenance", "question": "How often does my ZEEKR need servicing?", "answer": "ZEEKR vehicles need a scheduled service every 24 months or 30,000 km, whichever comes first. Cabin air filters may need replacing more often in dusty or high-pollution areas. Tyre rotation is recommended every 10,000 km."},
    {"id": "KB-10", "topic": "12V battery", "question": "My car says the 12V battery is low. What should I do?", "answer": "The 12V battery powers door locks, displays and control systems. If you see a low 12V warning, drive the car or keep it plugged in so the high-voltage battery can top up the 12V battery. If the warning comes back, book a 12V battery replacement; it takes about 30 minutes."}
  ]
}
